# apps/web is not prettier-formatted: it is written double-quoted and wider
# than printWidth 100, so `prettier --write` on any file there rewrites the
# whole file. Ignored until someone formats the tree in one deliberate commit.
apps/web/

# Generated by `renderWorkflow` and committed by `lurq autopilot init`. It must
# stay byte-identical to what lurq emits: reformatting it here would make this
# repository's copy diverge from what every user is handed, and the divergence
# would be invisible until someone compared them. lurq emits prettier's default
# double quotes, which is right for most repos — this one sets singleQuote, so
# its own generated file is the one file that cannot satisfy it.
.github/workflows/lurq-upgrade.yml
